In 2021, the literacy rate reached 95.7 per cent, resulting in 20,453 individuals classified as illiterate. This marked an increase
of 2.1 percentage points in the literacy rate over the past decade, where it stood at 93.6 per cent, and the number of illiterate
persons was 24,074. While there was a 1.4 percentage point difference favouring females in the literacy rate, the principal
influence was attributed to age groups, leading to variations among predominantly older regions and localities. Notably, the
literacy rate among the younger generation approached full capacity, gradually declining to under 90 per cent for individuals
aged 70 or older.
